  "result": "The 10-minute lesson on O3 is written, and I'm now finishing up. The files are written and I haven't proofread the lesson or counted its words.\n\n**Lesson:** `lessons/0001-context-and-memory-in-an-agent.html`\n\nIt has these parts:\n- **Warm-up:** a recall question from your agent-loop record.\n- **Context window:** the model keeps nothing between calls, so your program re-sends everything and you pay for it each call. There is a figure of context growing over four calls.\n- **When the window fills:** context rot, clearing old tool results, and compaction.\n- **Notes:** saving facts between sessions.\n- **Retrieval:** finding the right manual page, with a second figure showing the context window, notes and manual index.\n- **Worked example and practice:** the laser-cutter booking, with token counts compared against preloading a 40,000-token manual. The numbers are illustrative assumptions I chose, not measurements.\n- **Summary and sources.**\n\nFour short practice checks give immediate feedback. The primary source is Anthropic's \"Effective context engineering for AI agents\", which I fetched and read. The arXiv survey and the Elastic post are cited from search-result snippets only, so I haven't opened either page.\n\n**Also updated:** `RESOURCES.md` (new) and `NOTES.md`. I found no community link to cite, so the \"test it with others\" prompt points you to your team's design review instead.\n\nAsk me anything about the lesson in the chat. A quiz is ready when you want one, via `/quiz`.\n\nOne question for you: would you like the next lesson to go deeper on retrieval (chunking and search) or on deciding what to save as notes?",
